<title>USA: AlliedSignal, Aerospace Safety settle.</title>
<headline>AlliedSignal, Aerospace Safety settle.</headline>
<dateline>STRATFORD, Conn. 1996-10-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>AlliedSignal Inc and Aerospace Safety Technologies Inc said Wednesday they have reached a settlement in a patent infringement lawsuit.</p>
<p>Aerospace Safety, a subsidiary of Thermion Systems International, filed the lawsuit accusing AlliedSignal of improperly using its proprietary and patented electrothermal heating technology.</p>
<p>That technology is used to eliminate ice from aircraft surfaces.</p>
<p>The bulk of the agreement, which was described as &quot;amicable,&quot; has been deemed confidential.</p>
</text>
